{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_vkurxmtstltecta4dal2mebe3jv5x2yybsyg5i2vcbotnwkf4nnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Rust translation is complete. Summary of the implementation:\n\n**`Rect::new`** — Creates a new rectangle with given id, width, height, and default `RectOutInfo`.\n\n**`RectPacker::pack`** — Top-level packing routine that mirrors C's `rect_pack`:\n- Returns `true` for empty input\n- Sorts rectangles by max-side descending (tiebreak: min-side descending), matching `compare_rect_r_max_side`\n- Resets all `info` fields\n- Loops calling `pack_bin_tree`, advancing pages when paging is enabled, breaking when all fit, paging is disabled, or no rects fit\n\n**`pack_bin_tree`** (helper) — Mirrors the C `pack_bin_tree`: builds a root `BinNode` clamped to `max_w`/`max_h`, iterates from `next..=last`, and tries `find` then `grow` for each unpacked rect, tracking `next` while contiguously packed and updating `last` on the first failure.\n\n**`BinNode::find`** — Recurses into `right` then `down` for used nodes; returns `Some(self)` if unused and the rect fits.\n\n**`BinNode::split`** — Marks node as used and creates `down` (below) and `right` (to the right of) child nodes.\n\n**`find_and_split`** (private helper) — Mutable equivalent that descends, splits in place, and returns the chosen node. Needed because Rust's borrow checker disallows the C-style \"find then mutate\" pattern across recursive borrows.\n\n**`grow_right` / `grow_down`** — Take ownership of current state into `old`, expand the root in the chosen direction, attach `old` and a new sibling, then `find_and_split` for the rect.\n\n**`grow`** — Picks the direction using the same heuristic as C: prefer the \"should-grow\" direction that keeps the bin square-ish, otherwise fall back to whichever direction is feasible.\n\nAll five C unit tests (uniform paging, one-rect-per-page, fill, no-paging, fail-paging) plus the 10-iteration loop test of 199 rectangles produce identical results to the C version."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":164,"cache_read_input_tokens":35253,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":164,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6b760f1-ef43-4e57-83ba-a9b0f7a0157f","uuid":"eedffe66-77b9-4445-9abd-cd32ec12bc0c"}
